From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:06:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: t8132: Let the fault injector test the
 powered-down call net

With the colour and timing paths guarded, no kernel path sends a call to
a powered-down DCP any more. That leaves nothing that exercises the net
added in "Refuse a call to a powered-down DCP without failing the
session", so a regression in it would go unseen.

Add "call" to iomfb_m4_inject. While the DCP is powered down, it sends a
read-only call (A412, which the power-up also sends) and reports the
result. The write succeeds only if the call was refused with -EAGAIN and
the session is still healthy. Otherwise it returns -EIO, and the
quarantine that follows is the regression.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index 91b891c072..3f5f6e850e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -9487,7 +9487,9 @@ static const struct file_operations iomfb_m4_recover_fops = {
 /*
  * Fault injector for the recovery: "gated" quarantines a session that is
  * powered down, as a call to it did before such calls were refused;
- * "off" quarantines a running one with its display off.
+ * "off" quarantines a running one with its display off. "call" tests the
+ * net instead: it sends a read-only call (A412) to a powered-down DCP,
+ * which must be refused with -EAGAIN while the session stays healthy.
  */
 static ssize_t iomfb_m4_inject_write(struct file *file, const char __user *buf,
 				     size_t count, loff_t *ppos)
@@ -9508,9 +9510,20 @@ static ssize_t iomfb_m4_inject_write(struct file *file, const char __user *buf,
 		ret = dcp->gated ? 0 : -EAGAIN;
 	else if (sysfs_streq(cmd, "off"))
 		ret = !dcp->gated && dcp->display_off ? 0 : -EAGAIN;
+	else if (sysfs_streq(cmd, "call"))
+		ret = dcp->gated ? 1 : -EAGAIN;
 	else
 		ret = -EINVAL;
-	if (!ret) {
+	if (ret == 1) {
+		__le32 main_display = 0;
+		int call = dcp_m4_runtime_call(dcp->runtime, 412, false, NULL, 0,
+					       &main_display, sizeof(main_display));
+		int error = READ_ONCE(dcp->error);
+
+		dev_warn(dcp->dev, "injected call to a powered-down DCP: %d, session %s\n",
+			 call, error ? "failed" : "healthy");
+		ret = call == -EAGAIN && !error ? 0 : -EIO;
+	} else if (!ret) {
 		dev_warn(dcp->dev, "injected fault: %s\n", cmd);
 		dcp_m4_failed(dcp, -EPIPE);
 	}
-- 
